---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
import Switchboard from '../components/Switchboard.astro';
import { providers, track } from '../data/providers';
---

<Base
  title="Phone providers — Call Me Maybe"
  description="An honest comparison of SIP trunk providers that work with a home phone behind NAT: VoIP.ms, Telnyx, Flowroute. No affiliate links."
>
  <header class="lobby prov-hero" style="padding-block:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,4rem) 0;">
    <Switchboard class="prov-tangle prov-tangle--l" />
    <Switchboard class="prov-tangle prov-tangle--r" flip />
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Getting a number</p>
      <h1 class="wordmark" style="font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,3.6rem);">Providers</h1>
      <p class="tagline">
        You bring the number. Here is who to buy it from, what each one is good
        at, and where each one will annoy you.
      </p>
      <Divider />
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>One requirement decides everything</h2>
        <p>
          This phone lives behind your router with <strong>no ports open</strong>.
          It opens the connection outward and calls arrive back down that same
          pipe. So the only question that matters when shopping is:
        </p>
        <p class="prov-rule">
          <strong>Does the provider accept an outbound SIP registration?</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          If yes, it will work. If the provider only authenticates by pushing
          calls at a fixed IP address, it cannot work here without opening your
          network up — which is the thing this design exists to avoid. That
          rules out Twilio&rsquo;s Elastic SIP Trunking for this architecture,
          and it is not a criticism of Twilio; it is a different shape of
          product.
        </p>

        <h2 class="prov-h">Nobody is paying for this placement</h2>
        <p>
          There are no affiliate or referral links on this page. The programs
          exist and the traffic would be worth money, but the advice is worth
          more &mdash; the moment a recommendation carries a commission you have
          to wonder which it is. The links carry
          <code>utm_</code> parameters so we can see which providers people
          actually choose, and nothing else. If that ever changes it will say so
          here, in this paragraph, before anything else on the page.
        </p>
        <p>
          Rates move constantly, so no prices are quoted below. Every card links
          to the provider&rsquo;s own pricing page. Check it &mdash; a stale
          number on a page about honesty would be a poor joke.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="prov-list">
        {
          providers.map((p) => (
            <li class="prov-card">
              <div class="prov-head">
                <h3>{p.name}</h3>
                <span class="prov-tags">
                  {p.weUseThis && <span class="prov-tag prov-tag--ours">what we run</span>}
                  <span
                    class:list={[
                      'prov-tag',
                      p.registration === 'yes' ? 'prov-tag--ok' : 'prov-tag--todo',
                    ]}
                  >
                    {p.registration === 'yes' ? 'registration ✓' : 'unverified'}
                  </span>
                  <span class="prov-tag">{p.billing}</span>
                </span>
              </div>

              <p class="prov-summary">{p.summary}</p>

              <div class="prov-cols">
                <div>
                  <h4>Good</h4>
                  <ul>{p.pros.map((x) => <li>{x}</li>)}</ul>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <h4>Less good</h4>
                  <ul>{p.cons.map((x) => <li>{x}</li>)}</ul>
                </div>
              </div>

              <p class="prov-links">
                <a href={track(p.url, p.name.toLowerCase())} rel="noopener nofollow">
                  Open an account &rarr;
                </a>
                <a
                  href={track(p.pricingUrl, `${p.name.toLowerCase()}-pricing`)}
                  rel="noopener nofollow"
                >
                  Their rates &rarr;
                </a>
              </p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <h2>Evaluating one that is not listed</h2>
        <p>
          The list does not need to be exhaustive to be useful. Ask a prospective
          provider these, in order:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <strong>Registration or IP auth?</strong> If they cannot do
            registration, stop here.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Sub-accounts?</strong> The credential on the Pi should never
            be your portal login &mdash; if the Pi is compromised, you want to
            revoke one thing rather than everything.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Several numbers on one registration?</strong> This is what
            makes a second line cheap instead of a second trunk.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Prepaid or postpaid?</strong> Prepaid fails silently: the
            balance reaches zero and the phone simply stops ringing, which is
            indistinguishable from a quiet week. If prepaid, set up a balance
            alert on day one.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>E911?</strong> Decide deliberately. A house phone that
            cannot reach emergency services is a thing the people in that house
            should know about.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Found one that works? The runbook has a worked configuration, and a
          pull request adding a provider block is genuinely welcome &mdash; but
          please verify it against a live trunk first. A wrong example costs
          more than a missing one.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prov-hero {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .prov-hero > .wrap {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .prov-tangle {
    position: absolute;
    top: -2%;
    width: clamp(150px, 19vw, 290px);
    z-index: 0;
  }
  .prov-tangle--l {
    left: max(-3rem, -4vw);
  }
  .prov-tangle--r {
    right: max(-3rem, -4vw);
  }
  @media (max-width: 60rem) {
    .prov-tangle {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  .prov-rule {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: 1rem;
    font-size: var(--t-lg, 1.2rem);
  }

  .prov-h {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .prov-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .prov-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: clamp(1.1rem, 3vw, 1.75rem);
    background: var(--raised);
  }

  .prov-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .prov-head h3 {
    font-family: var(--display);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .prov-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .prov-tag {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .prov-tag--ok {
    border-color: var(--jade);
    color: var(--jade);
  }
  .prov-tag--todo {
    border-color: var(--accent-dim);
    color: var(--accent-dim);
  }
  .prov-tag--ours {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .prov-summary {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  .prov-cols {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem 2rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
  }
  .prov-cols h4 {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-soft);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .prov-cols ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .prov-cols li + li {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  .prov-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
</style>
